NTH cars — preparing for the advanced phase 2.","details":"Getting started with Ubuntu and the Linux environment.\n\nCore maths review: calculus, linear algebra, probability and statistics.\n\nROS 2 and its core concepts: Workspace, Package, Node, Topic, Service, Action.\n\nROS 2 programming in simulation, then connecting to real models such as drones and F1TENTH cars.","registerClosed":true},{"id":"ws26-machines","kind":"workshop","date":"14 Jan 2026","title":"Using the FabLab workshop machines","description":"For students who love making, engineering and DIY, or who need machines for course and personal projects. Participants learned the procedures and safety rules for working at FabLab and practised hands-on with basic mechanical machines, so they can use them confidently for study, research and building products.","time":"Wednesday, morning 9:00–11:00 am, afternoon 2:00–4:00 pm","venue":"Room 204, Block B11, EIU FabLab","registerClosed":true}]'))), '$.timeLabel', 'Time', '$.venueLabel', 'Venue', '$.feeLabel', 'Fee') END,
